    "updated_at": "2017-10-16T17:37:27Z",
    "body": "Dynamic `import()` is meant to match static `import`. It was specifically designed as a syntactic form to do so, based on our experience in e.g. Node.js with its context-sensitive `require()` and the use cases that enables. If you'd like to debate removing that feature, please open an issue on https://github.com/tc39/proposal-dynamic-import, where the appropriate community will be notified and be happy to help you understand.\r\n\r\n> It surprises me that these are different.\r\n\r\nWhy does it surprise you? You wrote the patch to explicitly reset the nonce to empty string for setTimeout. Which is what causes the failure.\r\n\r\n> I think that means we need to define an import mechanism that accepts nonces, not that we should treat these mechanisms as though they were nonced.\r\n\r\nIn general we don't distinguish between static and dynamic imports. Are you suggesting we make nonces unusable for module scripts, by removing nonce-propagation for *all* imports? I am pretty sure you are the one who wrote the nonce propagation part of the spec for imports in the first place, so this is a bit surprising to me.\r\n\r\nWe may eventually find a way to get TC39 to allow specifying nonces or other fetch options for individual imports, but last time I tried they rejected the idea in favor of out of band configuration, so I don't think that's going to happen any time soon.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
