    "updated_at": "2017-10-22T15:14:21Z",
    "body": "I know you mean well, but \"be happy to help you understand\" is rather condescending. I'm not sure Node.js really helps. You start hitting weird issues the moment you have multiple globals with different base URLs. Something you can only really get in the browser. And for static imports it makes some sense it's relative to the URL of the script, because those URLs are known at parse time, similar to CSS subresources. But dynamic import not matching `fetch()` will lead to confusion (e.g., when code in an `<iframe>` invokes some library code loaded in a parent).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
