    "created_at": "2017-11-08T18:09:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-11-08T18:09:13Z",
    "body": "Talked with @mikewest at TPAC, and we figured out that the way to get setTimeout to match eval is to *not* propagate parser metadata, but to propagate nonces. This is somewhat counterintuitive, but the idea is to minimize the \"new script-ness\" of the new script that setTimeout creates, even though that's how it works at a spec level. (And at the implementation level, in Chrome.) The way to do that is to propagate nonces (i.e. act as if it's the same script in a nonce-based CSP setting) but not propagate parser metadata (so that this new script doesn't need its own SRI hash in a hash-based CSP setting).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
